{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/923349-designing-packs-for-my-1656-poland-werewolf-game","id":923349,"title":"Designing Packs for my 1656 Poland Werewolf game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-29T10:29:01-07:00","id":923349,"title":"Designing Packs for my 1656 Poland Werewolf game","content":"So I have to come up with a few NPC packs for my Werewolf the Forsaken game and need a bit of help. There is a protectorate in the city of Gdansk currently and the leader of this protectorate is Mieczyslaw Iron Talon an Iron Master Alpha but I am having trouble coming up with ideas for his own pack and packs around the city. Any ideas would be gladly appreciated. Also I did have the idea that Mieczyslaw Iron Talon controlled several of the Granaries around Gdansk which in turn allows him to have his hands in the local economy. but a pack for each tribe is my top priority right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T11:55:01-07:00","id":923394,"title":"","content":"So he is called Iron Talon - WHY? What does his Deed Name tells you about him? His story will help you hammer his pack. And in long play, it will let you hammer Protectorate.<br /> <br /> Protectorate is alliance of packs, in the end. Have you got idea of packs taking it? They common theme will make Protectorate itself.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that Protectorates are not stable things - and not everyone need to join them. Thinking about those of Forsaken that <i>do not</i> join it, can also help you devise Protectorate itself.<br /> <br /> Gda\u0144sk of that era is known from merchants guilds - logically for Iron Masters in their midst would be to emulate them. Maybe general structure of Protectorate is that of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guild\" target=\"_blank\">Guild</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T12:40:06-07:00","id":923423,"title":"","content":"I'd guess Iron Talon might be the name because they keep a firm grip on their granaries.<br /> <br /> I don't know a whit about the political situation in 1656 Poland, apologies. One thing you might do is have Mieczyslaw be on top simply due to a grander ambition. They control some land, influence the economy, these are things not everyone really has the drive and capability to do. Because of this, they probably don't have a lot of 'slackers' in their pack, it either being made up of similarly ambitious-minded werewolves, or simply followers appreciating Iron Talon's power. If Iron Talon is the driving force behind the protectorate, it will probably be about something he's interested in. Alternatively, external enemies may have forced the protectorate to form. Aggressive and abundant Pure neighbors, an influx of shartha or something similar could all force packs to sort of band together, and if Iron Talon wants to maintain their temporal and economic power, they might tried to take charge to ensure that their interests are kept in mind. This might be painting them in an unflattering light, but without food and a thriving economy it's easy for territory to fall into doldrums.<br /> <br /> Again, pleading ignorance on the specific era and place, one thing to keep in mind is that packs don't necessarily form around tribes. It can be due to a place, a certain neighborhood that happened to spawn werewolves, religion, as werewolves from far and wide who may have settled in Gdansk and attended a certain church may find each other and prefer each others company. You might have some among the nobility, the military, immigrants. Packs can have members from all those castes. There's a seaport, right? It's possible to have a couple packs controlling that, perhaps protecting it from some marine threat, and maybe some packs who are constantly 'at sea' who they're closely allied with.<br /> <br /> One of the big things to remember when building a setting is you don't want to paint yourself in a corner or exhaust your possibilities. You don't have to name every member of every pack, or even every pack. Some are bound to stay out of peoples notice, maybe they're just so weak they don't bear mentioning, and even in in-world explanations you may not get entirely comprehensive lists, 'This is every pack in the city...' and may get more ambiguous with it. You might just pick a few noteworthy packs, like Iron Talon's and some the players are likely to run into, like neighbors, and develop a few exceptional members of each. Though, really, if you want to do it all go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T15:53:08-07:00","id":923538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/923349-designing-packs-for-my-1656-poland-werewolf-game?p=923394#post923394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So he is called Iron Talon - WHY? What does his Deed Name tells you about him? His story will help you hammer his pack. And in long play, it will let you hammer Protectorate.<br /> <br /> Protectorate is alliance of packs, in the end. Have you got idea of packs taking it? They common theme will make Protectorate itself.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that Protectorates are not stable things - and not everyone need to join them. Thinking about those of Forsaken that <i>do not</i> join it, can also help you devise Protectorate itself.<br /> <br /> Gda\u0144sk of that era is known from merchants guilds - logically for Iron Masters in their midst would be to emulate them. Maybe general structure of Protectorate is that of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guild\" target=\"_blank\">Guild</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Talon has that title because it is like iron fist, He was the one who formed the protectorate and allied it with the Kindred of Gdansk. It was formed for 3 reasons. 1. The Pure, the pure have always been in Poland of course but they where beaten back, but now with the Swedes invading the Pure who have followed have created an alliance with their Polish Kin and have been using the war to cleanse Poland of the Forsaken. Since Gdansk is one of the few cities that has not been burned down, so a protectorate was formed to defend the city. 2. The Spirits, the Spirits of Gdansk have become increasingly malevolent almost like something is poisoning them so an organized force had to be created to keep the spirits in line. 3. The Forsaken, Gdansk is a safe haven for the forsaken and of course this is beginning to bring overpopulation. The protectorate is there to keep packs in line, if you want to form a pack in Gdansk the protectorate enforces special rules on you, some may consider this tyrannical but it is necessary while you do not have to like the protectorate you have to respect it (think what the cammerilla did to every kindred in masquerade). Some packs have more power than others and it is a very unstable system but necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T23:36:28-07:00","id":923735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/923349-designing-packs-for-my-1656-poland-werewolf-game?p=923538#post923538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iron Talon has that title because it is like iron fist, He was the one who formed the protectorate and allied it with the Kindred of Gdansk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deeds Names are based on DEEDS - What exactly happen why rest of Uratha call him 'Iron Talon'? What is the tale about this events?<br /> <br /> Also, Deeds Name is mostly taken at introduction to Tribe - What is his story with Iron Masters then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/923349-designing-packs-for-my-1656-poland-werewolf-game?p=923538#post923538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Pure, the pure have always been in Poland of course but they where beaten back, but now with the Swedes invading the Pure who have followed have created an alliance with their Polish Kin and have been using the war to cleanse Poland of the Forsaken. Since Gdansk is one of the few cities that has not been burned down, so a protectorate was formed to defend the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then who will defend Gda\u0144sk now? I suspect Blood Talons to be joining with war on Pure. Envision one leader of thier faction in Protectorate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/923349-designing-packs-for-my-1656-poland-werewolf-game?p=923538#post923538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The Spirits, the Spirits of Gdansk have become increasingly malevolent almost like something is poisoning them so an organized force had to be created to keep the spirits in line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideal task for Bone Shadows - Who will lead them in city?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/923349-designing-packs-for-my-1656-poland-werewolf-game?p=923538#post923538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The Forsaken, Gdansk is a safe haven for the forsaken and of course this is beginning to bring overpopulation. The protectorate is there to keep packs in line, if you want to form a pack in Gdansk the protectorate enforces special rules on you, some may consider this tyrannical but it is necessary while you do not have to like the protectorate you have to respect it (think what the cammerilla did to every kindred in masquerade). Some packs have more power than others and it is a very unstable system but necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting - Could you expand on this? Put some examples?<br /> <br /> Also, can I make suggestion? You mentioned for now three Tribes that need to be in Protectorate to fullfil it's goals - Iron Masters, Bone Shadows and Blood Talons - other two are not so needed. <b>Maybe make them lesser factions that scrap for power in city, but have problem to aquire it?</b> This would piss off Storm Lords, but lead to more interesting setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, alliance with Kindred would be hard to swallow for Storm Lords in first place, take that in consideration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-30-2016, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T11:10:34-07:00","id":926523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/923349-designing-packs-for-my-1656-poland-werewolf-game?p=923735#post923735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deeds Names are based on DEEDS - What exactly happen why rest of Uratha call him 'Iron Talon'? What is the tale about this events?<br /> <br /> Also, Deeds Name is mostly taken at introduction to Tribe - What is his story with Iron Masters then?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then who will defend Gda\u0144sk now? I suspect Blood Talons to be joining with war on Pure. Envision one leader of thier faction in Protectorate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ideal task for Bone Shadows - Who will lead them in city?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is interesting - Could you expand on this? Put some examples?<br /> <br /> Also, can I make suggestion? You mentioned for now three Tribes that need to be in Protectorate to fullfil it's goals - Iron Masters, Bone Shadows and Blood Talons - other two are not so needed. <b>Maybe make them lesser factions that scrap for power in city, but have problem to aquire it?</b> This would piss off Storm Lords, but lead to more interesting setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, alliance with Kindred would be hard to swallow for Storm Lords in first place, take that in consideration. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Talon is an Elder Werewolf, an Elodoth of immense economic power. He has his Talons in the Merchants guild and gambling dens,granaries,distilleries, he has used this influence to combat spirit Urged and hosts throughout the city with an iron fist. So because of this he was given the title of Iron Talon by his tribe and it caught on. Some say he is a tyrant but he sees himself a hero<br /> <br /> The Blood Talons and the Gallows Post are working closely to defend the city, while The Post is mainly a Covenant of messengers they have become more martial in defending the city now the Post's hounds admire the Blood Talons and their fighting zeal. While not friends they have a mutual respect for one another. The Blood Talons leader is Amichai (means My People Are Alive in Hebrew) a Blood Talon of Jewish and Polish heritage who sees the bloodsuckers of Gdansk as a great weapon against the Pure, his hate of the Pure is legendary (probably masquerade breaking from the Kindreds point of view) who has gained the epithet The Gorehound because he lusts for the to bath in the Gore of Pure Uthra. He has even burned down a village just to kill one Pure.<br /> <br /> The Bone Shadows are tasked with keeping the spirits of the Shadow in line but now they are becoming more hostile for almost no apparent reason. So the Bone Shadow known as Balbina Grega has been coordinating her Tribe to begin mapping out the new locus points around the city and take excertions into the Shadow to find what has been causing this phenomenon. The main consensus on the alliance is one of fascination it allows the Bone Shadows to better understand the spirituality of the vampires and if they truly have a place outside of the flesh realm. Grega encourages her tribe to go to Kindred Elysium and to study the behaviors of the Muth Zuthuth.<br /> <br /> The idea I had for the Storm Lords is that they do have a presence in Gdansk but they mostly dwell among the minorities that are oppressed within Gdansk. Tatars, Cossacks, Russians, not to say all are apart of these groups but the majority descend from these minorities. There are Storm Lords who descend from non minority groups, the Storm Lords are divided on the alliance with the Kindred, some think it is a good idea to have less enemies so they can focus on their true enemies in the world. Others see this alliance as a show of weakness while they do not have any issue with the existence of the kindred they think that the Kindred are going to be a crutch for them to stand on. The leader of the Storm Lords is the Cossack Mykola a youngish Cahalith who has taken up the reigns since the death of his father at the hands of a Swedish Ivory Claw. He craves vengeance and has let it overwhelm him at times but it is possible that he may be too weak to actually fight the Ivory Claw and so he may deceive a group of young Kindred to go and fight the Claw to weaken his enemy before striking the killing blow.<br /> <br /> The Hunters in Darkness are probably the most content with the alliance they really do not care much for Kindred in general but now they can forge a closer alliance with them. There are several Kindred who live in Forests near sacred places locus points. Some of these kindred have been known in fact to use these places as worship sites because many of the hermits living out in the forests are members of the Old Faith covenant, a covenant I created to have the traditions of Tatar and Slavic culture be present. Mainly the group is a small covenant of Tatars and Pagans who practice a form of spiritual blood magic (not Cruac a custom power I am in the process of making, think Blood Tenebrous mixed with the rules of Cruac) which manipulates the shadow to some degree but also draws from something called the World Tree. Most Hunters would probably kill these Kindred but the packs have decided they will use this to their advantage and use these naive pagans as allies. Sort like &quot;We protect you and your sacred places and you help us kill the hosts and use the Locus's&quot;. Enough Hunters In Darkness do subscribe to the Pagan faith so the two can get along well. The Hunter's mainly want the western forest as territory but something else has claimed the west forest as domain, something otherworldly and not of the shadow. I was do not know really who would be<br /> <br /> Now of course there are the Ghost Wolves as well, but they are tribeless so they all form their own opinions on the Protectorate and the Kindred. The Protectorate laws and the Masquerade do apply to the Ghost Wolves and there is no beating around the bush, when a Ghost Wolf enters the city and makes their presence known they are invited to the manor of Iron Talon and told directly the Law, if it is broken they will suffer the wrath of not only the Protectorate but the Kindred as well.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}